  "mechanism": "The floor mesh active UV layer (exported as TEXCOORD_0, the layer the runtime samples and the bake writes to) is a collapsed layout: peds-fever floor has 32/56 vertices at (0,1) and 30/48 triangles with zero UV area. Cycles DIFFUSE bake writes nothing to degenerate UV triangles, so the bake covers only the small non-degenerate strip (u 0.125-0.375, v 0.361-0.389 -> the bright band at image row ~640), leaving ~99% of the image black. The mesh carries a non-degenerate full-square layer (TEXCOORD_1 -> UVMap.001) that the bake never used. Verified: trivial-material bake on the same geometry still produces 0.81 meanL (no lights in that isolation run), and swapping the active UV layer to the non-degenerate one flips the floor bake from meanL 2.21 to 246.55.",
